Make the chat-list preview item selection deterministic.

findGroupChatPreviews_, findDirectChatPreviews_ and findLocalChatPreviews_
picked the last chat item ordering only by the timestamp column, while the
canonical item queries (getChatItemIDs CRLast, get*ChatItemLast) order by
item_ts/created_at and chat_item_id.  When several items share the same
timestamp - a burst of internal items, e.g. the group feature items followed
by RGEMemberConnected - SQLite could return any of them, so the chat list
preview showed a group feature item ("SimpleX links: on", "Recent history:
off", "Direct messages: on") instead of the "connected" event.  Use the same
chat_item_id tie-break as the rest of the store.

Index: src/Simplex/Chat/Store/Messages.hs
--- src/Simplex/Chat/Store/Messages.hs.orig
+++ src/Simplex/Chat/Store/Messages.hs
@@ -806,7 +806,7 @@
             SELECT chat_item_id
             FROM chat_items ci
             WHERE ci.user_id = ? AND ci.contact_id = ct.contact_id
-            ORDER BY ci.created_at DESC
+            ORDER BY ci.created_at DESC, chat_item_id DESC
             LIMIT 1
           ) AS chat_item_id,
           COALESCE(ChatStats.UnreadCount, 0),
@@ -908,7 +908,7 @@
